<title>NORWAY: DnB 1996 pre-tax profits rise.</title>
<headline>DnB 1996 pre-tax profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31.</p>
<p>				  (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest income		     4,242     vs	4,347</p>
<p> Other operating income		  2,674     vs	2,770</p>
<p> Operating expenses			4,580     vs	4,939</p>
<p> Pre-tax op.profit before losses     2,337     vs	2,178</p>
<p> Pre-tax operating profit		2,724     vs	2,663</p>
<p> Tax						22     vs	    6</p>
<p> Net profit				  2,702     vs	2,657</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's largest commercial bank is Den norske Bank ASA (DNB). Seven analysts polled by Reuters had forecast pre-tax operating profits of 2,822 million crowns.  </p>
<p>Net profit from Vital</p>
<p> Forsikring				  56	  vs	  ---</p>
<p> Commission and fee income	  1,601	  vs	1,470</p>
<p> Commission expenses and fees paid  312	  vs	  303</p>
<p>Net profit on forex</p>
<p> and financial instruments	    715	  vs	  950</p>
<p> Net reversals on loans, guarantees 380	  vs	  479</p>
<p> EPS 1996 (crowns)			4.22	 vs	  N/A</p>
<p> Propsed dividend 1996 (crowns)     1.75	 vs	  1.5</p>
<p>--Rolf Soderlind, Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
